homelab-worker (0.1.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A finished job's output can be downloaded from any worker node (post-
    cutover item 51). The output is on the disk of the node that ran the
    job, and a download reaching another node failed with "output file is
    missing", so Drive's "download as zip" failed whenever it did. Each job
    now records its owner (output_node, migration 003), and a download for
    another node's file is relayed from that node, with the caller's own
    credential, once.
  * Only the owning node removes an expired job's file and row. The sweep
    on another node used to delete the row and leave the file on disk for
    good; a row whose owner has been gone a week is removed anyway.
  * A zip job fetches only https addresses with a public name: never an IP
    address, a fleet-internal name or the machine itself (item 53, defence
    in depth now that the api forwards no job creation). Checked when the
    job is created and again when it runs. jobs.zip_allowed_url_prefixes
    narrows it further.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 21:10:47 -0600

